course: dictionary
lesson: 8191
title: Making things right
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Restitution means giving back what was taken, or paying for harm you caused, so that things are made right. Saying sorry is a good start, but restitution goes further: you put the damage right.
explain: Look at the clue in «make full restitution (pay back all of it)». The words in brackets explain the phrase for you. Restitution is paying back all of it. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Restitution is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "a restitution". We say "make restitution", "pay restitution" or "restitution for damage". Notice the word "make" or "pay" goes with it.
fact: Restitution means giving back something that was stolen or lost to its owner, or paying for damage you caused.
fact: «Make full restitution» means pay back all of it.
fact: In law, a judge may order a wrongdoer to make restitution.
fact: In the Bible, Zacchaeus the tax collector promised to pay back four times what he had cheated people out of.
fact: Saying sorry is good, but restitution is making things right by repairing or repaying.
exercise: What does «make full restitution» mean? | Ask someone else to pay | Hide the thing you took | *Pay back all of it | Say sorry and forget about it
exercise: Sam kicked a ball and broke his neighbour's window. What would restitution be? | Breaking another window to even things up | Playing a different game | *Helping to pay for a new window | Only saying sorry
exercise: Which word means giving back what was taken or paying for harm you caused? | ancient | *restitution | festival | whisper
test: Mia took her friend's pencil case by mistake and lost a pen from it. What would restitution be for Mia? | *Giving back the case and paying for the lost pen | Hiding it in her bag | Asking her friend to pay her | Keeping the case because she is sorry
test: A judge ordered the man to make restitution. What did the judge want him to do? | Go on holiday | Write a poem about his crime | *Pay back the harm he had caused | Get a medal for good behaviour
exam: Which sentence uses restitution correctly? | The restitution was a sunny, warm day at the beach. | *After he broke the fence, he made restitution by paying for a new one. | Being kind to your pet is a form of restitution. | She has three restitutions in her bag.
